→ `backend/synthetics/beat_schedule.py`\n\nMy scope is specifically the `synthetics/state.json` file and ensuring the consecutive_failures tracking with 3-strike alert threshold works correctly.\n\nLet me verify the state.json file matches the contract exactly and check if there's anything missing from my scope. Looking at:\n1. NUTRIENTS.md §I.6 - the contract for state machine\n2. HYPHA-SYNTHETICS-CRAWLER.md - the specific state persistence section\n\nThe current `state.json` looks correct, but I should ensure it's properly validated. Let me also check if the CLI needs the crawler suite implementation (that seems to be the main gap):"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13332,"cache_read_input_tokens":63208,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":13332,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"652b4b3d-bcba-4c38-851d-efbb9fa0fa87","uuid":"a70c2c06-b405-4f99-85d1-b49254962c2f"}}
